   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <br><br>I have been running some models with INLA on a relatively large dataset. These models look something like Y ~ A + B + C + f(D, model = &#39;iid&#39;). In other words, there are 3 fixed effects, and one random effect. Y is binomial, and the full dataset is ~395,000 rows. <div><div><br></div><div>This model takes somewhere around 12hrs to run on 16 cores. </div><div><br></div><div>The error message arises when trying to add interactions between A, B, and C - specifically A:B, A:C, and B:C (no triple interaction!). On 16 cores, this model ran for over 48hrs before crashing with the following error message: </div></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">        GMRFLib\r\nversion 3.0-0-snapshot, has recived error no [21]<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">        Reason    : This should not happen<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">        Message   : Condition `density-&gt;Pinv&#39; is not TRUE<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">        Function  : GMRFLib_density_Pinv<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">        File      : density.c<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">        Line      : 1036<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">        RCSId     : file: density.c  hgid: b84cb08f11c9  date: Thu Jul 12 13:38:25 2018 +0300<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">Aborted (core dumped)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">..done<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">Error in inla.inlaprogram.has.crashed() : <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">  The\r\ninla-program exited with an error. Unless you interupted it yourself, please\r\nrerun with verbose=TRUE and check the output carefully.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:#c5060b\">  If this\r\ndoes not help, please contact the developers at &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">he...@r-inla.org</a>&gt;.</span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Consolas;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I&#39;d be interested in any feedback on what that error means, and how to potentially fix it. </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Additionally, I am wondering whether these computing times are to be expected with a dataset this size. <br><br>Thanks in advance!! <br>Romain</p></div></div>"
