   "id": "HHyp8vwaBwAJ",
   "from": "Romain Garnier",
   "author": "07419993cc085236",
   "date": "2019-03-18T16:10:33Z",
   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Error message clarification",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Just to post on quick update on this. <br><br>It turns out that the model needed to be specified using Ntrials in the call to INLA to speed up the calculation. The high number of non-unique cases in the relatively large dataset was making the computation difficult, ultimately resulting in the error above. <div><br></div><div>Reformatting the dataset to only include unique rows and a column containing the number of repeats for each works perfectly. </div><div><br></div><div>When specifying Y for this model, note that it needs to be the sum of the original Ys. For example, in the case of a binomial model, that means that it is either 0, or Ntrials (1 * number of cases). </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks again for all the help! </div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Thursday, March 14, 2019 at 4:44:25 PM UTC-4, INLA help wrote:</div></div>"
